WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.040
This November, Captain Marvel is going to
get pretty dark.

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:08.500
Marvel Comics recently announced a story arc
entitled "The Last Avenger," which will run

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.600
in the pages of Captain Marvel beginning with
issue #12.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:16.180
The arc will find Carol Danvers hunting down
her fellow Avengers, and at least one of them

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:18.380
will die by her hand early in the proceedings.

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:22.720
The official synopsis for the arc offers no
explanation other than to say that annihilating

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:24.660
the Avengers will be a pretty big deal:

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:27.100
"Captain Marvel has fought off alien hordes.

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:28.100
Rescued X-Men.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:29.360
Punched Thanos in the face.

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:30.760
Literally saved the world.

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:33.980
She now faces her greatest challenge: kill
the Avengers.

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:36.520
Has one of the world’s most powerful heroes
gone dark?

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:37.360
But why?

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:39.760
And what does this mean for Carol...for the
world?

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:41.700
Life on Earth will never be the same."

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:43.600
"Wait til you see this next one.

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:44.540
Everybody dies!"

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:45.280
"DUDE!

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:49.460
Maybe it won't get that bad, but as to why
she would be forced to turn against her teammates,

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:53.560
and even go so far as to execute one or more
of them, we can only guess.

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:57.300
It wouldn't be the first time, either; Marvel
fans know that Captain Marvel was forced to

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:00.200
fight her fellow heroes during the events
of Civil War 2.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:04.560
The arc comes courtesy of writer Kelly Thompson,
who has worked on a number of Marvel titles

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:08.640
including A-Force, Hawkeye, Jessica Jones,
and West Coast Avengers.

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:12.640
Thompson has been in charge of Captain Marvel
since the title's relaunch earlier this year,

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:16.399
and while she's had an awesome run, she's
the first to admit that she hasn't exactly

00:01:16.399 --> 00:01:20.130
conditioned readers to expect the kind of
mega-bomb she intends to drop on them with

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:21.300
issue #12.

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:23.900
Speaking with Comicbook.com, Thompson said,

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:28.030
"Carol is an incredibly powerful character
and you can really push her to the furthest

00:01:28.030 --> 00:01:31.490
edge, and you sort of need to in order to
keep things interesting, and that's what we're

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:33.320
trying to do with 'The Last Avenger.'

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:36.570
I think it's going to be a terrific Carol
story that really highlights her strengths

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:41.280
as a character, and maybe some weaknesses
as wel...It's a little risky but I'm excited.

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:42.660
I hope people love it."

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:47.020
We won't be able to crack open issue #12 until
it hits stands in November, but the synopsis

00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:51.899
for issue #13 was recently released as well,
and it clues us in to the fact that it's going

00:01:51.899 --> 00:01:54.280
to get pretty dark pretty fast, reading,

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.880
"One Avenger is dead at Captain Marvel’s
hand.

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:57.880
Who will be next?

00:01:57.880 --> 00:01:58.680
And why?

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:02.420
What strange allegiance is driving Captain
Marvel to the darkest edge?"

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:07.040
Marvel has a long history of good characters
going bad, from the iconic X-Men story arc

00:02:07.049 --> 00:02:11.410
"Dark Phoenix", which formed the basis for
this year's movie of the same name, to Spider-Man's

00:02:11.410 --> 00:02:14.040
tangle with the symbiote which would eventually
become Venom.

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:18.240
But the idea of Captain Marvel turning on
her friends is a truly scary one, especially

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:22.440
since she's one of the most insanely powerful
characters in the entire Marvel universe.

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:27.520
Just like her Marvel Cinematic Universe counterpart,
she has strength and durability on par with

00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:31.430
the Hulk, can discharge pure energy with perhaps
even more effectively than Thor, and can fly

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:32.700
faster than Iron Man.

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:36.860
She's a bit like all of the Avengers wrapped
into one, and if she's truly gotten it into

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:40.660
her head to wipe out Earth's Mightiest Heroes,
there might not be a heck of a lot anybody

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:41.660
can do to stop her.

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:45.450
Of course, Carol isn't just going to break
bad for no reason, and we can only guess as

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:46.640
to why she does.

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:47.800
Is it mind control?

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:49.960
A Captain Marvel from an alternate reality?

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:51.120
A really bad day?

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:52.360
An alien virus?

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:56.340
Or does this mysterious "allegiance" imply
that Carol isn't working on her own?

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:58.280
But who, and for what purpose?

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:02.840
Captain Marvel #12 hits stands and digital
platforms on November 20th, and that's when

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:03.860
the fun begins.

